{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the men turned from there, but Abraham still stood.</b> Even though the angels sent to destroy had already reached Sodom, Abraham still stood to seek mercy and to plead their merit, as the Sages of blessed memory said: \"Even if a sharp sword rests upon a man's neck, let him not withhold himself from mercy\" (Berakhot 10a). And likewise regarding those liable to execution they said: \"They return him even four or five times, provided there is substance to his words\" (Sanhedrin 44b)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:36.723019422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}